cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Acu361: an open, expert-annotated 3D atlas of the 361 WHO standard acupoints"
version: 1.0.0
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Elwyn921/Acu361"
url: "https://elwyn921.github.io/Acu361/"
abstract: >-
  3D coordinates of the 361 acupoints of the WHO Standard Acupuncture Point
  Locations in the Western Pacific Region (2008), 670 points in total, on the
  undeformed male standing body of the open anatomical model Z-Anatomy. All 361
  acupoints were located and finalized one by one by an acupuncturist in a 3D
  annotation tool; bilateral points are left-right symmetric, each right-side
  point being the mirror image of its left-side counterpart. The package also
  contains surface lines of the 14 meridians on the skin, the WHO proportional
  bone (skeletal) measurements in B-cun with endpoints on the body, and the
  seven anatomical layers of the body as GLB files.
keywords:
  - acupuncture
  - acupoints
  - meridians
  - WHO standard acupuncture point locations
  - 3D anatomy
  - Z-Anatomy
  - BodyParts3D
